# Keep the build context to what `npm run build` (strict typecheck + vite build) actually needs.
# `npm run typecheck` is `vue-tsc --build --force` against tsconfig.json, whose project references
# (tsconfig.app.json, tsconfig.node.json, tsconfig.e2e.json) span src/, tests/, scripts/, and every
# root-level *.config.ts -- not just src/ and public/ -- so those all have to stay in the build
# context. Only exclude what the build graph provably never touches: dependencies (reinstalled from
# the lockfile), build outputs, test/tooling run state, VCS/agent state, and docs/specs/ui_ux
# (markdown/CSS-reference content nothing in the TS project graph imports).

# Dependencies -- reinstalled from package-lock.json inside the image.
node_modules

# Build outputs -- (re)built inside the image; never trust a host-built dist/.
dist
dist-notation-harness
dist-workspace-harness

# Test/tooling run state and reports -- never inputs to `npm run build`.
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
coverage
.vitest
.vite
*.tsbuildinfo

# VCS and local agent/session/devcontainer state.
.git
.github
.agent
.devcontainer
.atd

# Local-only planning/notes files, not part of the shipped app or its build.
TODO.md
precusor.md

# Env/secrets -- this app makes no network calls and has no env-driven build config, but never send
# these into a build context regardless.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor/OS cruft.
.DS_Store
*.log

# Documentation/reference content: not part of the tsconfig project graph, so not needed to
# typecheck or build.
docs
specs
ui_ux
README.md
CODING_RULE.md
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md
LICENSE

# The Dockerfile/compose.yaml don't need to be inside their own build context (docker/ itself is
# kept -- the runtime stage COPYs docker/nginx.conf and docker/security-headers.conf directly).
Dockerfile
compose.yaml

